---
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import { organization, breadcrumbList, webSite } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'How We Test | Marqly';
const description =
  'How Marqly evaluates every bookmark manager, web clipper and read-it-later app we write about: the hands-on protocol, how prices are verified, how we stay independent, and how to flag a correction.';
const canonical = 'https://www.marqly.com/how-we-test';
const updated = '2026-10-05';

const jsonLd = [
  organization(),
  webSite(),
  breadcrumbList([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'How we test', path: '/how-we-test' },
  ]),
];
---

<LandingLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="head">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>How we test</span>
        </nav>
        <h1>How we test</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          When a Marqly page says we compared, reviewed or “ranked” tools, this is the process
          behind that claim. It exists so you can judge our conclusions — and so we can be held to
          them. If any detail here is wrong, <a href="mailto:support@marqly.com">tell us</a> and we
          will correct it and date the change.
        </p>
        <p class="updated" data-date={updated}>Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>October 5, 2026</time></p>
      </header>

      <section class="prose">
        <h2>What we actually do before writing</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>We use the real product.</strong> Every tool we recommend in a “best of” or
            comparison is installed and driven through the exact task the article is about — importing
            a messy bookmark export, clipping a page, searching for something you half-remember. We do
            not rank a product from its marketing page alone.</li>
          <li><strong>We test the free tier unless we say otherwise.</strong> Most readers start on a
            free plan, so our headline verdicts are earned on the free tier. Where a conclusion depends
            on a paid feature, the sentence names the plan.</li>
          <li><strong>Same inputs across tools.</strong> For comparisons we feed each product the same
            set of URLs and the same saved items, so differences reflect the product rather than what
            happened to be easy to save that day.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How prices and claims are verified</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Prices and platform support come from the vendor’s own pricing or product page, checked
            on a specific date, and shown as “as of &lt;date&gt;”. Competitor data in our comparison
            pages is reviewed on a dated cycle and we publish the date.</li>
          <li>Product-shutdown and acquisition facts are cited to the vendor or an official notice, not
            to rumor round-ups.</li>
          <li>If we cannot verify a number, we leave it out rather than estimate it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Independence and how Marqly appears in our own lists</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Marqly is the product this site is about, so we are <em>not</em> a neutral third party and
            we won’t pretend to be. That is exactly why we state plainly where a competitor is better:
            “best for” notes say when you should pick someone else.</li>
          <li>Marqly is not automatically first in every ranking. A product is placed by how it fits the
            job the page is solving, and competitor tools lead their own pages.</li>
          <li>We do not accept payment for placement, and a listed tool’s rank does not change because a
            vendor contacted us. There are no affiliate links in our editorial rankings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Ratings and reviews</h2>
        <p>
          We do not publish star ratings for our own product in structured data, and we do not fabricate
          aggregate scores. When we mention a store rating we tie it to the store, the platform and a
          date. Review claims about other tools are summarised from hands-on use and named public
          sources, not invented.
        </p>

        <h2>Updates, corrections and dates</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every editorial page carries a visible <strong>“Updated”</strong> date that matches the
            page’s structured-data <code>dateModified</code>. We change that date only when the substance
            changes — not to chase search results.</li>
          <li>Factual corrections are free and fast. Email <a href="mailto:support@marqly.com">support@marqly.com</a>
            with the page and the wrong detail; if it is genuinely wrong we fix it and note the change.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What this page does <em>not</em> promise</h2>
        <p>
          We do not run a laboratory with a fixed panel of reviewers or publish raw benchmark datasets
          for every article. Where a page does cite a measured test (for example our AI retrieval
          benchmark), the page links the method and results directly, so that claim is backed by the
          test rather than by this generic policy.
        </p>

        <p class="cta">
          Read the method behind a specific verdict on the
          <a href="/blog/best-pocket-alternatives-2026">Pocket-alternatives rundown</a>, the
          <a href="/alternatives">alternatives hub</a> or the
          <a href="/compare">comparison pages</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</LandingLayout>

<style>
  .page { background: var(--surface-1, #fff); }
  .wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-16, 4rem) var(--space-5, 1.25rem) var(--space-24, 6rem); }
  .head { margin-bottom: var(--space-8, 2rem); }
  .crumbs { font-size: var(--fs-sm, .875rem); color: var(--ink-3, #6b7280); margin-bottom: var(--space-4, 1rem); }
  .crumbs a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--ink-1, #111); text-decoration: underline; }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4, 1rem); color: var(--ink-1, #101014); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-lg, 1.125rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-2, #374151); margin: 0 0 var(--space-3, .75rem); }
  .updated { font-size: var(--fs-sm, .875rem); color: var(--ink-3, #6b7280); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--fs-h3, 1.35rem); margin: var(--space-10, 2.5rem) 0 var(--space-3, .75rem); color: var(--ink-1, #101014); }
  .prose p, .prose li { line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-2, #374151); }
  .prose a { color: var(--ink-1, #101014); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .prose a:hover { color: var(--accent, #0071e3); }
  .prose ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .prose li { margin: .4rem 0; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; background: var(--surface-2, #f3f4f6); padding: .1em .35em; border-radius: 4px; }
  .cta { margin-top: var(--space-8, 2rem); }
</style>
